From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gerard Marull-Paretas <gerard@teslabs.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:52:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: input: touchscreen: hynitron,cst816x: Add supply

The controllers run from a single 2.8 V to 3.6 V supply. Boards may
switch it, for example along with the display panel the touchscreen
is laminated to, so document it.

This patch was prepared with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude
Code, using Claude Opus 5.5), which wrote the change and this commit
message under the submitter's direction. It was reviewed by the
submitter, who takes responsibility for it.
---
 input/touchscreen/hynitron,cst816x.yaml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/input/touchscreen/hynitron,cst816x.yaml b/input/touchscreen/hynitron,cst816x.yaml
index df52431b1d49..ae8424693534 100644
--- a/input/touchscreen/hynitron,cst816x.yaml
+++ b/input/touchscreen/hynitron,cst816x.yaml
@@ -30,6 +30,9 @@ properties:
   reset-gpios:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  vdd-supply:
+    description: Power supply of the controller.
+
   linux,keycodes:
     minItems: 1
     items:
@@ -60,6 +63,7 @@ examples:
             interrupt-parent = <&gpio0>;
             interrupts = <4 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
             reset-gpios = <&gpio 17 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+            vdd-supply = <&vdd_ts>;
             touchscreen-size-x = <240>;
             touchscreen-size-y = <240>;
             linux,keycodes = <KEY_UP>, <KEY_DOWN>, <KEY_LEFT>, <KEY_RIGHT>,
